# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Source of truth for the UI translation catalogue.

The ENGLISH STRING IS THE KEY (see src/i18n.h). Add a language by adding its
code to LANGS and a column to CAT (or, for a language translated as one block,
a mapping like ZH below, merged in emit()); run this to regenerate
src/i18n_catalogue.h.
A blank translation is legal and means "not translated yet" -- tr() falls back
to English, so a partial column ships safely.

Terminology follows the established CAD vocabulary of each language rather than
a literal rendering: fillet is "Redondeo"/"Conge"/"Verrundung", not "relleno".
Spanish and Portuguese are LATIN AMERICAN / BRAZILIAN, matching where the users
asking for this actually are.
"""
